1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,800
One of the most common misconceptions in
systems engineering is that verification

2
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:11,165
and validation only happen at the very
end, once a physical system has been

3
00:00:11,165 --> 00:00:16,965
built. In ISO 15288 and INCOSE Handbook,
confirmation is not a final gate — it is

4
00:00:16,965 --> 00:00:22,185
built directly into the exchanges between
the Technical Processes. <break

5
00:00:22,185 --> 00:00:23,200
time="1.2s" />

6
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:27,663
Let us trace how the Technical Processes
transform an initial problem into an

7
00:00:27,663 --> 00:00:31,950
operational system. <break time="0.8s" />
Business or Mission Analysis and

8
00:00:31,950 --> 00:00:36,001
Stakeholder Needs and Requirements
Definition establish the Life cycle

9
00:00:36,001 --> 00:00:40,053
concepts and Stakeholder needs and
requirements. <break time="0.9s" />

10
00:00:40,053 --> 00:00:44,868
System Requirements Definition translates
those into technical System requirements.

11
00:00:44,868 --> 00:00:49,449
<break time="0.8s" /> System Architecture
Definition and Design Definition turn

12
00:00:49,449 --> 00:00:53,677
them into a System architecture
description, a System design description,

13
00:00:53,677 --> 00:00:58,022
and a System interface definition. <break
time="0.9s" /> Implementation and

14
00:00:58,022 --> 00:01:02,133
Integration build and assemble the
Integrated system or system element.

15
00:01:02,133 --> 00:01:06,184
<break time="0.8s" /> Finally,
Transition, Operation, Maintenance, and

16
00:01:06,184 --> 00:01:10,706
Disposal deliver the Installed system,
run the Operational system, sustain it,

17
00:01:10,706 --> 00:01:12,820
and retire it. <break time="1.3s" />

18
00:01:12,888 --> 00:01:17,156
Now notice the crucial point in the
digital model: <break time="0.6s" /> you

19
00:01:17,156 --> 00:01:21,253
do not wait for the Integrated system to
start checking your work. <break

20
00:01:21,253 --> 00:01:25,179
time="0.8s" /> Intermediate artefacts
along the entire chain flow into

21
00:01:25,179 --> 00:01:29,674
Verification and Validation long before
manufacturing begins. <break time="1.3s"

22
00:01:29,674 --> 00:01:29,788
/>

23
00:01:29,871 --> 00:01:34,268
Look first at the Verification loops
below the spine. <break time="0.8s" />

24
00:01:34,268 --> 00:01:38,724
Verification checks technical correctness
against specified criteria. <break

25
00:01:38,724 --> 00:01:43,121
time="0.7s" /> System Requirements
Definition sends System requirements and

26
00:01:43,121 --> 00:01:47,518
Verification criteria, and receives
Verified system requirements in return.

27
00:01:47,518 --> 00:01:52,153
<break time="0.9s" /> System Architecture
Definition and Design Definition send

28
00:01:52,153 --> 00:01:57,025
their architecture, design, and interface
descriptions, and receive Verified system

29
00:01:57,025 --> 00:02:00,946
architecture and design. <break
time="0.9s" /> And once Integration

30
00:02:00,946 --> 00:02:05,343
delivers the Integrated system or system
element, Verification produces the

31
00:02:05,343 --> 00:02:09,859
Verified system and Verification report
for Transition and Validation. <break

32
00:02:09,859 --> 00:02:10,691
time="1.3s" />

33
00:02:10,756 --> 00:02:14,733
Now look above the spine at the
Validation loops. <break time="0.8s" />

34
00:02:14,733 --> 00:02:18,766
Validation checks whether we are still
building the right system for its

35
00:02:18,766 --> 00:02:22,913
intended purpose. <break time="0.7s" />
Stakeholder Needs and Requirements

36
00:02:22,913 --> 00:02:27,231
Definition sends Stakeholder needs and
requirements with Validation criteria,

37
00:02:27,231 --> 00:02:31,719
and receives Validated stakeholder needs
and requirements. <break time="0.9s" />

38
00:02:31,719 --> 00:02:35,980
Architecture and Design artefacts are
validated as well, returning Validated

39
00:02:35,980 --> 00:02:40,070
system architecture and design before a
single component is built. <break

40
00:02:40,070 --> 00:02:44,217
time="0.9s" /> Later, Validation confirms
both the Verified system and the

41
00:02:44,217 --> 00:02:48,024
Installed system from Transition,
releasing the Validated system and

42
00:02:48,024 --> 00:02:50,296
Validation report. <break time="1.3s" />

43
00:02:50,361 --> 00:02:55,765
And whenever either process uncovers a
gap, both Verification and Validation

44
00:02:55,765 --> 00:03:01,385
feed Constraints on solution straight
back to all upstream definition processes

45
00:03:01,385 --> 00:03:06,789
and System Analysis. That is how ISO
15288 turns intermediate artefacts into

46
00:03:06,789 --> 00:03:12,048
an early-warning network, catching flawed
assumptions when change is still

47
00:03:12,048 --> 00:03:12,841
affordable.

